# Commit built binaries with their source changes

Every project in this repo ships its build output. When the user asks to commit and/or push:

- Stage and commit modified built artifacts for the project(s) being committed, e.g. `go/*/bin/**`, `ps/gf/gf.exe`, `python/tp/tp.exe`, `python/tp/tp.pyz`.
- Never exclude them as "unrelated", "binary rebuilds", or noise. They are meant to ship.
- Prefer the same commit as the source/docs/tests that produced them. If a prior commit left them out, commit and push them promptly as a follow-up.
- Changes belonging to a different, unrelated project may still be excluded — the binaries of the project being committed may not.

Rebuild ownership varies (see project-specific rules such as Larry): whether or not you run the build, commit whatever binaries are already modified in the working tree.
